no one has higher hopes than the studio  when it comes to a movies franchise  potential if they sense a feature could  be the start of something major  they might even greenlight a follow up  before the film even hits theaters but  in some cases those sequel plans are  embarrassingly premature here's some  movies that were so bad their sequels  were actually canceled the Mortal  Instruments City of Bones the successes  of Twilight and the hunger games made  adaptations of young adult novels hot in  Hollywood  Sony seemed poised to capitalize by  bringing Cassandra Clare's The Mortal  Instruments City of Bones to the big  screen with plans to follow with the  second installment city of ashes  unfortunately for the studio the film  was a disaster with critics and  audiences earning back just above half  of its production costs instead the  series was adapted to the small screen  as the TV series Shadowhunters Fantastic  Four Fox's 2015 reboot of Fantastic Four  may have seemed like a good idea at the  time especially since it boasted a  quartet of critically favorite actors  and Michael B Jordan miles teller Jamie  Bell and kate mara critics  overwhelmingly hated it however and the  box office results were terrible a  sequel is slated for 2017 but it never  went into production John Carter  Disney's John Carter was such a  box-office bomb that the film's title is  now often used as an adjective to  describe a grossly underperforming  picture the film's critical reception  was moderate at best but would really  destroyed the would-be franchise was how  much of a loss the studio took at the  box office the film reportedly cost a  whopping 250 million dollars to make not  counting its marketing expenses and  earned just 73 million in North America  ouch Green Lantern although Ryan  Reynolds has since proven his worth in  the superhero market by way of Deadpool  his turn as the Green Lantern was a  franchise non-starter and remained  something of a star in his filmography  Green Lantern tanked the box office at  Green Lantern 2 lost its greenlight  Terminator Genisys 2015's terminator  genisys couldn't quite recapture the  fanfare of the original series even with  the reappearance of Arnold  Schwarzenegger as the titular Terminator  as an added boost the movie performed  poorly with critics and domestic  audiences which made the cancellation of  its sequel plans far from surprising The  Cat in the Hat  adaptations of dr. Seuss's books have  usually done well including How the  Grinch Stole Christmas horton hears a  who and Lorax but critics and audiences  rejected the 2003 live-action take on  one of Zeus's most iconic properties The  Cat in the Hat the film scored just 10  percent on Rotten Tomatoes and  financially underperformed as well Sue's  widow Audrey Geisel went so far as to  refuse any further live-action films  Battlefield Earth John Travolta's  unintentionally hilarious costume was  the least of battlfield Earth's problems  this infamous dud which was supposed to  be followed up with a sequel to cover  the rest of l ron hubbard's 1000 page  plus sci-fi epic was laughed off by  reviewers and largely ignored by  audiences Tron Legacy it took more than  two decades for the first sequel to  1982's Tron to come down the pike and it  looks like it might take just as long  for the next one the 2010 movies  domestic box-office was mostly a bust  and despite an animated TV spin-off  Disney abandoned plans for another movie  thanks for watching subscribe to our  YouTube channel to watch more videos of  the one you just saw and leave us a  comment to let us know which scrapped  sequel you'd most love to see someday
 

